  m_Name: PatClin1
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: "You are discussing treatment options with your doctor, and he mentions
    a phase III clinical trial as a potential option for you. You\u2019ve heard of
    clinical trials, but naturally, you still have questions.\r\n\r\n<b>Clinical
    trials are only for patients who don\u2019t have other treatment options.</b>\r\n\r\nIs
    this <b>true</b> or <b>false?</b>"
  explanation: "Clinical trials can offer new opportunities for patients at many
    stages of disease \u2013 sometimes even as a first treatment, not just when other
    options haven\u2019t worked. These trials test whether a new treatment may work
    better than the current standard, so patients may be offered a trial treatment
    alongside, or instead of, existing options."
  correctAnswer: False
  incorrectAnswer1: True
  incorrectAnswer2: 
  incorrectAnswer3: 
  questionRole: Patient
  questionType: TrueFalse
  questionStage: Clinical
